00:06:12.586 --> 00:06:13.710
So what's behind that demo?

00:06:13.710 --> 00:06:15.390
How did I make that happen?

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:17.054
How do we get it to talk?

00:06:17.054 --> 00:06:18.720
So let's dive into
that and take a look.

00:06:22.810 --> 00:06:25.290
So the first thing we used
in there was Dialogflow.

00:06:25.290 --> 00:06:27.732
So the challenge
here is, how do we

00:06:27.732 --> 00:06:29.190
build that
conversational front end

00:06:29.190 --> 00:06:31.050
so that it can
respond to questions

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:32.760
and have answers and
keep track of what

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:34.200
people are doing in there?

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:36.810
So that's where
Dialogflow comes in.

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:41.550
So Dialogflow-- let
me go over here--

00:06:41.550 --> 00:06:44.740
Dialogflow is where we're
going to build natural and rich

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:46.520
conversational experiences.

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:48.070
So this is going to
give us a new way

00:06:48.070 --> 00:06:50.150
to interact and build products.

00:06:50.150 --> 00:06:52.845
It's going to use
conversational AI on there

00:06:52.845 --> 00:06:54.970
to make sure that we're
having a good conversation.

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:57.250
So what we build in
here can be deployed

00:06:57.250 --> 00:06:58.690
to a number of different places.

00:06:58.690 --> 00:07:01.750
We can deploy it to
the Google Assistant,

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:04.510
to Alexa, to Facebook
Messenger, on Slack,

00:07:04.510 --> 00:07:05.770
other places like that.

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:07.270
So that's where
we're going to build

00:07:07.270 --> 00:07:10.620
this rich conversational
experience.

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:15.700
So if you want to learn this,
take a look at dialogflow.com.

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:16.740
There's a blog on there.

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:18.520
There's some docs on there.

00:07:18.520 --> 00:07:21.370
I worked through some tutorials
to get up to speed on this.

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:23.119
So if I wanted to build
something in here,

00:07:23.119 --> 00:07:26.500
I'm going to click over
here on Go to Console.

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:28.444
From within there, I'm
put into this place

00:07:28.444 --> 00:07:30.110
we're I'm going to
build an application.

00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:33.739
So there's a few things
in here to talk about.

00:07:33.739 --> 00:07:35.530
Intents are things that
we're going to say.

00:07:35.530 --> 00:07:37.120
This is what we plan to do.

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:40.012
So which classes are
available on Friday?

00:07:40.012 --> 00:07:42.220
I want to know which classes
are available on Friday.

00:07:42.220 --> 00:07:44.120
That's my intention.

00:07:44.120 --> 00:07:44.860
There's Entities.

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:47.020
Entities are things
that the system knows

00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:49.750
about-- a particular date
or the name of a class

00:07:49.750 --> 00:07:50.950
or something like that.

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:53.200
There's a number of
built-in system entities,

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:57.370
and then there are also custom
ones that you can define.

00:07:57.370 --> 00:08:00.205
Fulfillment is where this
would go to be fulfilled.

00:08:00.205 --> 00:08:02.080
In this case, it's going
to be a webhook that

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:04.030
calls out to Apigee Edge.

00:08:04.030 --> 00:08:06.140
And then Integrations is
where we'll deploy this.

00:08:06.140 --> 00:08:07.420
So that's going to be
the different devices

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:08.470
this can run on.

00:08:08.470 --> 00:08:10.270
I'll dive into each
of these individually,

00:08:10.270 --> 00:08:12.320
and we'll take a look at that.

00:08:12.320 --> 00:08:14.590
So let's start with Intents.

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:17.440
So you heard me say, which
classes are available?

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:19.870
So within Intents, what
we're going to do is,

00:08:19.870 --> 00:08:23.200
these are different things
that people would say.

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:25.330
We'll start with where
I started with this--

00:08:25.330 --> 00:08:26.060
I give it a name.

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:27.550
Which Classes When
is what I chose

00:08:27.550 --> 00:08:29.630
to call this particular intent.

00:08:29.630 --> 00:08:33.140
And it has an input context
and it has an output context.

00:08:33.140 --> 00:08:35.351
So the input
context is something

00:08:35.351 --> 00:08:37.350
that would constrain
whether it's called or not.

00:08:37.350 --> 00:08:39.880
A certain condition must
be met or Dialogflow

00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:41.770
has to be in a particular
state before this

00:08:41.770 --> 00:08:43.054
is allowed to be called.

00:08:43.054 --> 00:08:45.220
In this case, this is one
of the first things that's

00:08:45.220 --> 00:08:47.050
going to be asked,
so I haven't put

00:08:47.050 --> 00:08:48.640
any kind of input
context in there

00:08:48.640 --> 00:08:50.306
that would constrain
how this is called.

00:08:50.306 --> 00:08:52.482
Because I want it to
be called immediately.

00:08:52.482 --> 00:08:54.190
Next, down here I've
got an output state.

00:08:54.190 --> 00:08:55.630
So after this has
been completed,

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:58.930
the state of the system is
"asked which classes when."

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:00.760
And this five over
here is the duration.

00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:03.530
That's how long this
context will stay in memory.

00:09:03.530 --> 00:09:05.620
There's also some parameters
associated with this,

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:06.460
like the date.

00:09:06.460 --> 00:09:10.230
So when I say next Tuesday or on
Friday, it will remember that.

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:12.730
And it's going to keep that in
context, so that I don't have

00:09:12.730 --> 00:09:14.470
to keep saying
Tuesday every time

00:09:14.470 --> 00:09:17.170
I want to talk to the device.

00:09:17.170 --> 00:09:18.700
The next thing to
look at in here

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:20.170
are these training phrases.

00:09:20.170 --> 00:09:23.080
So what you do is you type in
a few examples of how somebody

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:24.470
might interact with this.

00:09:24.470 --> 00:09:26.650
So, what classes are
offered tomorrow?

00:09:26.650 --> 00:09:28.570
Tell me which classes
are offered tomorrow.

00:09:28.570 --> 00:09:30.760
Which classes are
available today?

00:09:30.760 --> 00:09:34.432
What classes are available
on Tuesday or Monday?

00:09:34.432 --> 00:09:35.140
Things like that.

00:09:35.140 --> 00:09:37.120
Which classes are
open on Monday?

00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:40.260
These are all examples of ways
that people would say this.

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:42.010
Now, the great thing
here is this does not

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:43.300
have to be an exact match.

00:09:43.300 --> 00:09:46.210
It's helpful if it's close, but
it doesn't have to be exact.

00:09:46.210 --> 00:09:48.130
You'll notice that
some of these things

00:09:48.130 --> 00:09:49.480
are highlighted in yellow.

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:52.600
Those are entities that
Dialogflow has spotted for me.

00:09:52.600 --> 00:09:54.434
So this maps to a date.

00:09:54.434 --> 00:09:55.600
This is going to be sysdate.

00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:57.490
So when I say
tomorrow, it's going

00:09:57.490 --> 00:10:00.010
to map that to a particular
calendar date for me

00:10:00.010 --> 00:10:03.180
and it's going to put
that into a parameter.

00:10:03.180 --> 00:10:05.290
So that's what the
yellow is in here.

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:08.340
The next thing down here
is Actions and Parameters.

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:10.850
So when somebody
asks this question,

00:10:10.850 --> 00:10:14.030
I don't have the answer right
here in this particular spot.

00:10:14.030 --> 00:10:16.640
I need to go call a system
and get this information.

00:10:16.640 --> 00:10:18.710
When they ask what
classes are available,

00:10:18.710 --> 00:10:21.710
I need to go do a query and
look up a list of classes,

00:10:21.710 --> 00:10:23.870
find that, translate it
into the right format,

00:10:23.870 --> 00:10:25.790
and then return
it to this system.

00:10:25.790 --> 00:10:30.170
So what I've got in here
is, Find Which Classes

00:10:30.170 --> 00:10:32.330
is the name of the action.

00:10:32.330 --> 00:10:34.790
And then there's some
parameters that get sent over

00:10:34.790 --> 00:10:36.510
to my webhook with that.

00:10:36.510 --> 00:10:39.597
So I'd like to send the
date and the date original.

00:10:39.597 --> 00:10:41.180
And the difference
between those two--

00:10:41.180 --> 00:10:44.600
the date is a particular
calendar date and date original

00:10:44.600 --> 00:10:45.530
is how they asked.

00:10:45.530 --> 00:10:47.840
So if they said next
Tuesday or Friday,

00:10:47.840 --> 00:10:50.760
that's the words that
they used for that.

00:10:50.760 --> 00:10:53.234
And then if I can't get an
answer from an external system,

00:10:53.234 --> 00:10:54.650
I want to have a
fallback in here.

00:10:54.650 --> 00:10:56.233
And I'm going to
say, sorry, I was not

00:10:56.233 --> 00:10:57.980
able to find which
classes are available

00:10:57.980 --> 00:11:00.140
on that particular date.

00:11:00.140 --> 00:11:01.610
So these are the parameters.

00:11:01.610 --> 00:11:03.180
That's the action.

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:06.500
These are some responses
that would get called.

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:08.900
If you know the answer--
like if they say thank you,

00:11:08.900 --> 00:11:11.814
you can say you're welcome,
right here with just this.

00:11:11.814 --> 00:11:13.730
If it needs to call out
to an external system,

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:15.950
we're going to come down
here under Fulfillment

00:11:15.950 --> 00:11:17.491
and we're going to
slide this slider.

00:11:17.491 --> 00:11:19.674
It says Enable webhook
call for this intent.

00:11:19.674 --> 00:11:21.590
And that means it's going
to call your webhook

00:11:21.590 --> 00:11:24.090
and it's going to pass these
parameters and this action word

00:11:24.090 --> 00:11:27.180
in a JSON body where
you can process it.

00:11:27.180 --> 00:11:29.920
So that's one intent
that's in here.

00:11:29.920 --> 00:11:31.380
A few others that
I have in here--

00:11:31.380 --> 00:11:33.700
you can do things
like find class times.

00:11:36.280 --> 00:11:38.270
Sorry, let's look
at another one here.

00:11:38.270 --> 00:11:40.840
Let's find classes when.

00:11:40.840 --> 00:11:45.140
So you can ask when a class
is, a particular class.

00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:47.665
And then we can sign up
for a particular class--

00:11:50.345 --> 00:11:52.660
Book a class.

00:11:52.660 --> 00:11:54.210
Now, notice on this
one that there's

00:11:54.210 --> 00:11:55.543
a constraint on the way in here.

00:11:55.543 --> 00:11:57.910
There's a context that
has to be fulfilled

00:11:57.910 --> 00:11:59.000
before we get into here.

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:03.310
So they have to have asked when
the classes are before they

00:12:03.310 --> 00:12:04.467
can sign up for one.

00:12:04.467 --> 00:12:06.800
That's just something I put
in here to demonstrate that.

00:12:06.800 --> 00:12:08.920
So this context
has to be satisfied

00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:10.390
before this will
even be considered

00:12:10.390 --> 00:12:13.602
as an answer to something
somebody is asking.

00:12:13.602 --> 00:12:15.310
And there are some
examples-- register me

00:12:15.310 --> 00:12:17.560
for spinning on Tuesday,
register me for the yoga

00:12:17.560 --> 00:12:19.270
class on Tuesday at 9:00 AM.

00:12:19.270 --> 00:12:23.080
So there are a few different
ways they can talk to this.

00:12:23.080 --> 00:12:24.912
These checkboxes
down here in Actions,

00:12:24.912 --> 00:12:26.620
they mean that these
things are required.

00:12:26.620 --> 00:12:28.572
So if they forget to
put those in there,

00:12:28.572 --> 00:12:29.530
we want to prompt them.

00:12:29.530 --> 00:12:32.620
So if they don't tell us what
the day is, for example, we're

00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:34.730
going to say, on which day?

00:12:34.730 --> 00:12:36.710
And we're going to
prompt them for that.

00:12:36.710 --> 00:12:40.420
And then once we get the
answer, it will continue.

00:12:40.420 --> 00:12:43.390
Similar to the last one, we're
going to pass a date, a time,

00:12:43.390 --> 00:12:46.680
and we're going to pass a
class name in this case.

00:12:46.680 --> 00:12:49.760
So those are the intents
that I have built into here.

00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:51.810
Next thing to look
at are entities.

00:12:51.810 --> 00:12:56.240
So the yellow ones in
here are built-in ones.

00:12:56.240 --> 00:12:59.090
The purple in here, or
the pink in here, that

00:12:59.090 --> 00:13:00.350
is a particular time.

00:13:00.350 --> 00:13:01.760
Those are system ones.

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:06.590
These brownish ones over here,
these are different entities

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:07.580
that I've defined.

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:10.520
So it knows about regular system
things that typically pop up

00:13:10.520 --> 00:13:12.175
in conversations.

00:13:12.175 --> 00:13:13.550
But there are some
things that it

00:13:13.550 --> 00:13:14.925
doesn't know about,
that you want

00:13:14.925 --> 00:13:16.290
to define for your application.

00:13:16.290 --> 00:13:18.470
So in my case, I have
names of classes,

00:13:18.470 --> 00:13:21.170
like yoga and spinning
and cardio boxing

00:13:21.170 --> 00:13:22.370
and things like that.

00:13:22.370 --> 00:13:24.630
I need to tell it
about those things.

00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:26.270
So I've come over
to Entities here,

00:13:26.270 --> 00:13:28.640
and I've created a new
entity called A Class Name.

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:31.230
And that's going to
describe that class.

00:13:31.230 --> 00:13:33.110
So within there, I'm
going to list these out.

00:13:33.110 --> 00:13:35.060
These are different
ways somebody

00:13:35.060 --> 00:13:37.070
might describe a class.

00:13:37.070 --> 00:13:38.840
Kickboxing, yoga,
indoor cycling--

00:13:38.840 --> 00:13:40.850
those are ways that they
might describe them.

00:13:40.850 --> 00:13:42.680
You can also define
synonyms over here.

00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:44.360
So someone might
describe kickboxing

00:13:44.360 --> 00:13:46.550
as kickboxing or cardio boxing.

00:13:46.550 --> 00:13:49.640
Indoor cycling might be indoor
cycling, spinning, or biking--

00:13:49.640 --> 00:13:52.080
those are all different
ways they could do that.

00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:53.600
And if we check
this box up here,

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:56.360
Allow automated expansion,
what that's going to do

00:13:56.360 --> 00:13:59.110
is that's going to use
the AI and the speech APIs

00:13:59.110 --> 00:14:01.052
in Google Cloud and
that's going to make it

00:14:01.052 --> 00:14:03.260
so it will recognize these
other things that are also

00:14:03.260 --> 00:14:07.970
similar to this that we didn't
necessarily list in here.

00:14:07.970 --> 00:14:11.060
So that's how we enter
entities in here.

00:14:11.060 --> 00:14:13.540
The next thing to look at
is Fulfillment in here.

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:16.780
So, how do we get an answer
when somebody asks a question?

00:14:16.780 --> 00:14:20.050
When they ask what classes
are available on Friday,

00:14:20.050 --> 00:14:21.490
how do we get an
answer for that?

00:14:21.490 --> 00:14:23.920
So we're going to call
out to the webhook here,

00:14:23.920 --> 00:14:25.906
and it's going to respond.

00:14:25.906 --> 00:14:27.280
So within there,
we've got a URL.

00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:28.930
This is Apigee
Edge in this case.

00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:31.570
And that is my API
proxy that's going

00:14:31.570 --> 00:14:33.790
to go and find answers for me.

00:14:33.790 --> 00:14:35.950
I need to send in
an API key in order

00:14:35.950 --> 00:14:38.290
to get validated by that
system and to identify

00:14:38.290 --> 00:14:40.190
what this agent is.

00:14:40.190 --> 00:14:42.080
So we're going to have
an API key in here

00:14:42.080 --> 00:14:43.871
and that's going to be
passed in and that's

00:14:43.871 --> 00:14:45.560
going to identify this system.

00:14:45.560 --> 00:14:48.280
The other option in here is to
write the code right down here

00:14:48.280 --> 00:14:49.240
in the inline editor.

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:51.220
So you can write Cloud
Functions for Firebase,

00:14:51.220 --> 00:14:52.870
they can be hosted down there.

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:54.730
And you can run it
straight inline.

00:14:54.730 --> 00:14:56.770
I'm interested in the
Apigee Edge application

00:14:56.770 --> 00:14:59.110
here, because I'm integrating
with an existing system.

00:14:59.110 --> 00:15:03.257
And I've got a great way to
map this request into that.

00:15:03.257 --> 00:15:05.090
And finally, we've got
Integrations in here.

00:15:05.090 --> 00:15:07.590
So this is where we would deploy
this once it's all written.

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:09.660
So you get it all up
and running and working,

00:15:09.660 --> 00:15:13.040
then you deploy it on a
particular device or platform.

00:15:13.040 --> 00:15:15.790
So in my case, I'm running
it on the Google Assistant.

00:15:15.790 --> 00:15:17.680
That's the first option here.

00:15:17.680 --> 00:15:20.080
We could run it inside a web
page, Facebook Messenger,

00:15:20.080 --> 00:15:21.820
Slack, a few other
options in there.

00:15:21.820 --> 00:15:24.220
So there's a lot of different
choices for where we

00:15:24.220 --> 00:15:27.656
deploy this and how it works.

00:15:27.656 --> 00:15:29.030
So what would I
do at this point?

00:15:29.030 --> 00:15:31.770
I built these intents,
I've got some entities,

00:15:31.770 --> 00:15:33.460
I've set up some
fulfillment, I've

00:15:33.460 --> 00:15:36.070
got a few integrations
checked in there.

00:15:36.070 --> 00:15:37.150
How do I test this out?

00:15:37.150 --> 00:15:39.520
Well, it turns out there's
a nice testing harness right

00:15:39.520 --> 00:15:40.840
in here.

00:15:40.840 --> 00:15:42.455
And one nice thing
about this is this

00:15:42.455 --> 00:15:44.080
is going to show us
the details of what

00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:46.970
that body will be that's
sent over to the webhook.

00:15:46.970 --> 00:15:49.750
So let's find out what classes
are available on Friday.

00:15:56.160 --> 00:15:57.360
So I type that in there.

00:15:57.360 --> 00:15:59.477
It's going to make a call out.

00:15:59.477 --> 00:16:01.810
And it's going to get a context
back and an answer back.

00:16:01.810 --> 00:16:03.960
So what we see here is,
I asked what classes

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:05.430
are available on Friday.

00:16:05.430 --> 00:16:07.770
And it answered with,
yoga, indoor cycling,

00:16:07.770 --> 00:16:10.260
kickboxing are
available on Friday.

00:16:10.260 --> 00:16:11.760
And it also set a context--

00:16:11.760 --> 00:16:14.310
asked which classes when.

00:16:14.310 --> 00:16:17.050
And it sent this
over to Apigee Edge.

00:16:17.050 --> 00:16:20.422
It processed it, it found
an answer, and it returned.

00:16:20.422 --> 00:16:22.380
The way I figured out
what it was going to send

00:16:22.380 --> 00:16:24.960
was I clicked down here
on Diagnostic Info.

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:27.000
And there's the
JSON body of what's

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:28.240
going to be sent over there.

00:16:28.240 --> 00:16:31.310
So the interesting
parts of this are

00:16:31.310 --> 00:16:33.290
we're going to see
within here query result,

00:16:33.290 --> 00:16:35.170
we're going to see an action.

00:16:35.170 --> 00:16:38.830
So the action was
find which classes.

00:16:38.830 --> 00:16:41.640
And then the date down here
