00:16:41.640 --> 00:16:43.470
And then this is how
I spoke that date.

00:16:43.470 --> 00:16:49.869
I said on Friday, I
didn't say 2018, 5, 11.

00:16:49.869 --> 00:16:51.410
And then we can see
the response that

00:16:51.410 --> 00:16:53.229
comes back from the system.

00:16:53.229 --> 00:16:54.770
It's going to set
a context, and it's

00:16:54.770 --> 00:16:57.614
going to return a few more
parameters at the bottom there.

00:16:57.614 --> 00:17:01.050
[CLEARS THROAT] Excuse me.

00:17:01.050 --> 00:17:03.930
So that's our basic information
that gets sent back and forth.

00:17:03.930 --> 00:17:06.411
I use this to try and figure
out what I should send over

00:17:06.411 --> 00:17:08.369
to Apigee Edge and how
to process it and things

00:17:08.369 --> 00:17:10.000
like that.

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:12.660
So if we continue
our conversation,

00:17:12.660 --> 00:17:14.430
we know which classes
are available,

00:17:14.430 --> 00:17:16.190
let's find out when
yoga is offered.

00:17:23.700 --> 00:17:26.310
Now, it remembers that the
first time I asked about Friday,

00:17:26.310 --> 00:17:27.960
so I didn't have to
say Friday again.

00:17:27.960 --> 00:17:29.410
I just said, when
