00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:34.290
at 9:00 AM, 11:00
AM, and 6:00 PM.

00:17:34.290 --> 00:17:35.790
It's important in
these applications

00:17:35.790 --> 00:17:37.650
to keep that
context, so somebody

00:17:37.650 --> 00:17:41.340
doesn't have to keep asking the
same thing over and over again.

00:17:41.340 --> 00:17:44.080
When we have a conversation
with another person,

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:46.420
this implied context
is in the conversation.

00:17:46.420 --> 00:17:48.792
So if I say, hey, what's
available on Friday?

00:17:48.792 --> 00:17:51.000
The next time I ask, let's
just assume that I'm still

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:52.560
talking about Friday.

00:17:52.560 --> 00:17:55.470
So that date is stored
in the output context

00:17:55.470 --> 00:17:58.140
from the first call, and
it's sent into the parameters

00:17:58.140 --> 00:18:00.180
of the second call.

00:18:00.180 --> 00:18:02.761
And again, we can look down
here at Diagnostic Info

00:18:02.761 --> 00:18:05.010
and we can get an idea of
what's going to be sent over

00:18:05.010 --> 00:18:07.059
to our webhook for fulfillment.

00:18:07.059 --> 00:18:08.100
So here we are down here.

00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:10.350
The action this time
is find class times.

00:18:10.350 --> 00:18:12.790
The specific class name is yoga.

00:18:12.790 --> 00:18:14.220
And here's the
two different ways

00:18:14.220 --> 00:18:16.230
we specify the date-- the
calendar date and then

00:18:16.230 --> 00:18:18.889
how I spoke that the first time.

00:18:18.889 --> 00:18:21.180
And we see the answer that
comes back from the back end

00:18:21.180 --> 00:18:21.846
system in there.

00:18:24.367 --> 00:18:25.450
So that's our information.

00:18:25.450 --> 00:18:28.497
That's how we're going
to work with Dialogflow.

00:18:28.497 --> 00:18:29.580
Looks good here, you know?

00:18:29.580 --> 00:18:32.130
It looks like this is
doing exactly what I want.

00:18:32.130 --> 00:18:34.020
The next step would
be to figure out

00:18:34.020 --> 00:18:35.640
how to map that to
a back end system.

00:18:35.640 --> 00:18:38.110
And we'll dive into
