00:18:46.860 --> 00:18:48.680
and it's going to
work in either case.

00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:54.160
So the webhook
request and response

00:18:54.160 --> 00:18:56.780
flow, the way to look at that--

00:18:56.780 --> 00:18:58.780
I went and looked at the
reference documentation

00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:00.370
on this to figure
out how to do this.

00:19:00.370 --> 00:19:05.290
So go over to dialogflow.com,
look at the documentation,

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:08.350
click over to Reference,
scroll down to Webhook Request

00:19:08.350 --> 00:19:09.587
and Response.

00:19:09.587 --> 00:19:11.170
So here's the request
for the webhook.

00:19:11.170 --> 00:19:12.640
It tells you what
that format is.

00:19:12.640 --> 00:19:17.590
You've got to pass in a session,
a response ID, a query result.

00:19:17.590 --> 00:19:19.524
I'm sorry, that's the--
yeah, in the request.

00:19:19.524 --> 00:19:21.190
And then there's some
details under here

00:19:21.190 --> 00:19:21.970
of what the object is.

00:19:21.970 --> 00:19:23.150
And you can click
through on that

00:19:23.150 --> 00:19:24.566
and it'll give you
all the details

00:19:24.566 --> 00:19:25.840
on that particular thing.

00:19:25.840 --> 00:19:27.850
On the response
side, we're going

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:29.680
to see that this
text comes back.

00:19:29.680 --> 00:19:32.440
So we can have
text that's spoken

00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:34.820
and we can also have text
that's shown on the screen.

00:19:34.820 --> 00:19:36.839
So for some of
these integrations,

00:19:36.839 --> 00:19:38.380
like if we're using
Slack or if we're

00:19:38.380 --> 00:19:41.630
using the assistant on
a phone, for example,

00:19:41.630 --> 00:19:45.000
we can return a series of cards
with possible answers on there.

00:19:45.000 --> 00:19:47.650
We can return images,
URLs, things like that.

00:19:47.650 --> 00:19:49.390
Or we can just have
fulfillment text,

00:19:49.390 --> 00:19:52.490
if we're speaking to
