00:19:52.490 --> 00:19:54.130
So that's our
request and response

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:58.010
and that's the reference
on how that works.

00:19:58.010 --> 00:20:00.970
So the next tool to look
at is the existing service.

00:20:00.970 --> 00:20:03.190
So we've got an existing
service in there

00:20:03.190 --> 00:20:06.097
and we want to call
that existing service

00:20:06.097 --> 00:20:07.930
and we want to have it
give us answers back.

00:20:07.930 --> 00:20:09.520
So let's explore
what that looks like.

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:14.762
So here's our existing service.

00:20:14.762 --> 00:20:16.720
What I've got here on
the screen is just a tool

00:20:16.720 --> 00:20:21.050
that I use to call RESTful
services and get answers back.

00:20:21.050 --> 00:20:23.080
So in this case, I've
got a URL up here

00:20:23.080 --> 00:20:25.550
and my response
comes back over here.

00:20:25.550 --> 00:20:28.060
So if I call my back
end system and it's

00:20:28.060 --> 00:20:31.000
going to talk to
the classes API,

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:33.160
we're going to pass
